<title>SWITZERLAND: Dutch, UK economies performing well - Tietmeyer.</title>
<headline>Dutch, UK economies performing well - Tietmeyer.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank president Hans Tietmeyer said Europe's economic situation was differentiated, but growth in the United Kingdom was likely to continue and the Dutch economy was performing well.</p>
<p>Tietmeyer was speaking as chairman of the G10 central bank governors' committee, following the G10 central bankers' regular monthly meeting.</p>
<p>&quot;All in all the Dutch economy is performing well,&quot; Tietmeyer said, adding, there was a likelihood that growth in the UK would continue. -- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
